      "node_type": "function",
      "name": "_state_snapshot",
      "line_number": 60,
      "docstring": "Trim the full L4 state to a stable subset suitable for deterministic testing.\n\nWe purposely include only the main L2 outputs and a few key\nhigh-level fields. Volatile or heavy telemetry (e.g., route_trace,\npatch_log, correction_journal) is omitted from the snapshot.\n\nSnapshot shape:\n    {\n      \"strategy_result\": ...,\n      \"rag_result\": ...,\n      \"bullet_result\": ...,\n      \"draft_result\": ...,\n      \"qa_result\": ...,\n      \"safety_result\": ...,\n      \"hil_result\": ...,\n      \"meta_learning_result\": ...,\n      \"multi_agent\": ...,\n      \"self_correction\": ...,\n      \"summary\": ...,\n    }",
      "imports": [],
      "dependencies": [],
      "responsibility_level": "L5",
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "node_type": "class",
      "name": "Scenarios",
      "line_number": 103,
      "docstring": "Houses all simulation scenarios used for deterministic CI testing.\n\nEach scenario:\n    \u2022 Builds an initial_state dict.\n    \u2022 Invokes run_workflow_v10_9(initial_state).\n    \u2022 Returns an object with top-level fields + trimmed state snapshot.",
      "imports": [],
      "dependencies": [],
      "responsibility_level": "L5",
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "node_type": "class",
      "name": "Engine",
      "line_number": 468,
      "docstring": "Simulation execution engine.\n\nProvides:\n    \u2022 run(name, overrides=None)\n    \u2022 run_all()\n    \u2022 list()\n    \u2022 sync wrappers\n\nThis is a META-level test harness for CI and regression scenarios.",
      "imports": [],
